{% comment %}
  Prefix for asset and page URLs.

  In production this stays the absolute site URL, which is what GitHub Pages,
  jekyll-feed and jekyll-sitemap expect.

  Under `jekyll serve` it resolves to just the baseurl (empty on this site), so
  every {{ base_path }}/... reference becomes root-relative (/assets/...).

  Without this split a local server emits HTML that links the *deployed*
  stylesheet and scripts. _sass edits then appear to do nothing, images that
  exist only locally 404, and any script that has not been pushed yet 404s with
  them — which is what silently removed the projects page filter buttons, since
  they ship `hidden` and are revealed by assets/js/portfolio-filter.js.
{% endcomment %}
{% if jekyll.environment == "development" %}
  {% assign base_path = site.baseurl %}
{% elsif site.url %}
  {% assign base_path = site.url | append: site.baseurl %}
{% else %}
  {% assign base_path = site.github.url %}
{% endif %}